    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "6fa97791a4a71755f6281f994d7faac1462b5da19a0068f5ae67e725ddf8d022",
      "text": "Today brings two wonderful destinations. After breakfast, you drive for about 1 hour to Areguá and the beautiful Lake San Bernardino, a peaceful lake cradled in green hills.\n\nFrom there, you continue for 2 more hours to Vista Alegre Natural Resort, nestled in Colonia Independencia in the Guairá region. This resort is a true paradise spanning around 200 hectares of forests, hills, ravines, waterfalls, and trails, all surrounded by stunning natural scenery. You sleep in cosy rustic-style cabins, bungalows, or villas, some with their own pool and barbecue area. In the afternoon, you explore the Cordillera del Ybituruzu, the highest mountain range in Paraguay. Its trails wind through the mountains towards hidden waterfalls and breathtaking viewpoints, where the vibrant greens of the forest stretch out against the wide blue sky. In the evening, you dine at the resort.",
